| `tests.durations` | integer | `10`; absent, 10, which the loader reports as `[using default] tests.durations = 10` | a whole number, 1 or more; 0 is refused because pytest uses it to report every duration | `make test`, through `scripts/config_get.py` and the `scripts/config_loader.py` KEYS row | Sets how many slowest test durations `make test`, and therefore `make verify`, reports with `--durations`. A wrong type or a value below 1 refuses before pytest starts. | selecting tests: the full gate still includes `slow` tests; `make unit` skips them | always |
